task:
Alert: Network anomaly detection: WS-RIYER-01 made periodic outbound HTTPS connections at roughly 5-minute intervals between 13:30 and 14:10 UTC on 2026-11-10. Review activity between 13:20 and 14:20 UTC and decide whether it is malicious.

Environment context (from the organization's asset and service inventory):
Organization: Lakeview Accounting (domain LAKEVIEW-ACCT / lakeview-acct.local), a small accounting office.
Hosts: workstations WS-DWELLS-01 (dana.wells, accountant), WS-RIYER-01 (raj.iyer, analyst), WS-KORTEGA-01 (kim.ortega, IT administrator), WS-TNGUYEN-01 (tara.nguyen, help desk); servers DC-LV-01 (domain controller, DNS), FILE-LV-01 (file server, finance shares, scheduled jobs), PROXY-LV-01 (explicit web proxy, port 8080; all web egress goes through it). There is no VPN; remote administration is only done from WS-KORTEGA-01 inside the office.
Accounts: kim.ortega is the only IT administrator. tara.nguyen (help desk) can create domain accounts but is not an administrator. Service accounts: svc-backup (Vaultline backup agent on FILE-LV-01) and svc-reporting (ReportSync job on FILE-LV-01, runs every minute and re-authenticates on each run).
Change calendar for 2026-11-10: the svc-reporting password is scheduled to be rotated by IT at 13:30 UTC (CHG-2291); the ReportSync job on FILE-LV-01 must then be updated manually with the new password. Monthly workstation patching by IT is scheduled during business hours.
IT practices: kim.ortega patches workstations by remotely running \\FILE-LV-01\IT\scripts\Install-MonthlyPatches.ps1 with PowerShell from WS-KORTEGA-01. The help desk creates temporary contractor accounts on request, always named temp.<name>, added only to the Contractors domain group; temporary accounts never receive administrator rights. No other account creation is expected.
Approved software and services: Microsoft 365 / OneDrive; Vaultline (vaultline-backup.com) offsite backup; DataGrid Analytics desktop (installed in C:\Program Files\DataGrid\Analytics\ on analyst workstations), whose updater dgupdate.exe checks update.datagrid-analytics.com over HTTPS about every 5 minutes. No other file-sharing, cloud-storage or remote-access services are approved.

Objective: Determine whether the available security evidence supports a malicious-activity finding, a benign disposition, or an insufficient-evidence determination.

Evidence is available only through these tools: list_sources, query, get_record. Retrieve evidence with the tools before answering. You may make at most 30 tool calls.

Respond with a single JSON object (no prose, no code fences) that conforms to this JSON schema. Output only the instance, not the schema:
{
 "type": "object",
 "additionalProperties": false,
 "required": [
  "assessment",
  "confidence",
  "supporting_observations",
  "known_telemetry_limitations",
  "claims_not_established",
  "recommended_action",
  "additional_evidence_needed"
 ],
 "properties": {
  "assessment": {
   "type": "string",
   "enum": [
    "malicious",
    "benign",
    "insufficient_evidence"
   ]
  },
  "confidence": {
   "type": "number",
   "minimum": 0,
   "maximum": 1,
   "description": "Probability that the assessment is correct."
  },
  "supporting_observations": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
     "claim",
     "claim_type",
     "record_ids"
    ],
    "properties": {
     "claim": {
      "type": "string"
     },
     "claim_type": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
       "observed_fact",
       "inferred_claim"
      ]
     },
     "record_ids": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
       "type": "string"
      }
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "known_telemetry_limitations": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "claims_not_established": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "string"
   },
   "description": "Material questions the available evidence cannot answer."
  },
  "recommended_action": {
   "type": "string",
   "enum": [
    "close",
    "escalate",
    "collect_more"
   ]
  },
  "additional_evidence_needed": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "string"
   }
  }
 }
}

attempts.answer:
{
  "assessment": "malicious",
  "confidence": 0.8,
  "supporting_observations": [
    {
      "claim": "At 14:05 UTC, the domain controller issued Kerberos tickets for kim.ortega from IP 10.20.10.22, and FILE-LV-01 recorded a successful network logon by kim.ortega from that same IP. The available host telemetry maps 10.20.10.22 to WS-RIYER-01, while the stated remote-administration practice permits administration only from WS-KORTEGA-01.",
      "claim_type": "inferred_claim",
      "record_ids": ["S04-00274", "S04-00275", "S04-00276", "S04-00326"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The workstation’s connection records show recurring connections through the proxy at roughly five-minute intervals during the alert period, including 13:40:29, 13:45:50, 13:50:33, 13:55:37, 14:00:15, and 14:05:05 UTC. These records identify the proxy endpoint, not the ultimate HTTPS destinations.",
      "claim_type": "observed_fact",
      "record_ids": ["S04-00158", "S04-00189", "S04-00236", "S04-00243", "S04-00254", "S04-00267"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The domain controller logged credential-validation events for raj.iyer with FILE-LV-01 and WS-DWELLS-01 as the respective workstations; these records do not include a result establishing whether validation succeeded.",
      "claim_type": "observed_fact",
      "record_ids": ["S04-00063", "S04-00212"]
    }
  ],
  "known_telemetry_limitations": [
    "The workstation-filtered DNS and TLS queries returned no records in the requested window, so this evidence does not identify the periodic HTTPS destination, SNI, or certificate.",
    "The connection records show traffic from WS-RIYER-01 to the internal proxy at 10.20.20.30:8080, not direct connections to external hosts.",
    "The FILE-LV-01 security record establishes a network logon but does not show the commands, files, or administrative actions performed in that session."
  ],
  "claims_not_established": [
    "The identity of the external destination contacted at the alert’s recurring intervals.",
    "Whether the periodic connections were generated by the approved DataGrid updater or another process.",
    "Whether kim.ortega's credentials were compromised, or whether the FILE-LV-01 logon from WS-RIYER-01 had an authorized explanation.",
    "Whether data was accessed, changed, or exfiltrated during the observed activity."
  ],
  "recommended_action": "escalate",
  "additional_evidence_needed": [
    "Proxy logs for 13:30–14:10 UTC, including full destination, user, request, and TLS inspection details for WS-RIYER-01.",
    "Endpoint process, command-line, and network telemetry on WS-RIYER-01 for the recurring connection times, including evidence for dgupdate.exe.",
    "FILE-LV-01 process, PowerShell, SMB, and file-access auditing around the 14:05 kim.ortega logon.",
    "Confirmation from IT whether kim.ortega used WS-RIYER-01 or whether the logon was otherwise authorized, and review of the svc-reporting rotation and ReportSync job update records."
  ]
}
